<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aricia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aricia was an ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alban-hills">Alban Hills</a> south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, near modern Ariccia. Close to the sanctuary of Diana at Lake Nemi, it was a meeting place of the Latin League. Around 504 BCE the Latins, aided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristodemus-of-cumae">Aristodemus of Cumae</a>, defeated an Etruscan army there. It later became a Roman municipium on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appian-way">Via Appia</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the early Republic it brought Diana from <b>Aricia</b> to the Aventine, Castor from Tusculum and Fortuna Primigenia from Praeneste; Camillus promised Juno of Veii a temple if she deserted her city, took Veii in her name and dedicated her temple on the Aventine.</blockquote><a href="/religion/roman-religion">Roman religion · Spread</a></li><li><blockquote>Aristodemus of Cumae and the Latins defeated an Etruscan army at <b>Aricia</b> around 504 BCE, and in 474 BCE Hiero I of Syracuse, allied with Cumae, destroyed an Etruscan fleet off Cumae, dedicating captured helmets at Olympia, one of them now in the British Museum.</blockquote><a href="/culture/etruscans">Etruscans · Contact &amp; Exchange</a></li><li><blockquote>The tyrant Aristodemus defeated the Etruscans at <b>Aricia</b> around 504 BCE, and in 474 BCE Cumae and Hieron I of Syracuse destroyed an Etruscan fleet off the city.</blockquote><a href="/state/cumae">Cumae</a></li><li><blockquote>By the 6th century BCE they met in council at the grove of Ferentina and dedicated a federal shrine of Diana at <b>Aricia</b>, whose founding a Latin dictator, Egerius Baebius of Tusculum, is said to have led.</blockquote><a href="/state/latin-league">Latin League</a></li></ul></section>
